One entry fails, and is out of both baselines. eval-group-13's rule

    RULE { ?t ?st ?n } WHERE {
        ?t rdf:type :Team
        GROUP BY ?t ?st { ?t :owns ?c . ?c :status ?st } [ ?n := COUNT(*) ]
    }

has a variable predicate in its head, so it can generate a triple that matches
?t :owns ?c in its own group pattern. Under the specification's Rule Dependency
section that is a closed dependency on itself, and the rule set is not
stratifiable, so it has no inference graph to compare. sqlib refuses it. The
test needs WHERE DATA, or a constant predicate in the head, in #1380.

